Z||000010||Alex4mula||06-06-2001||07:50 AM||||Here is mine. Sluppy was my inspiration. Thanks!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">Looked at his picture several times while doing it. I did one piece for the center section and one piece each for each side. Not difficult but time consuming and painful in the back.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/pde2ed0e8449533dab8adfbbee5ac3953/fe6d7729.jpg.orig.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/pe1ed96cd99ba531c2959a9c8cd3a75b3/fe6d7728.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Carrolles||06-06-2001||10:28 AM||||If you flip the spare tire upside down you'll gain some room to store emergency stuff.  I keep a gallon of anti-freeze, a quart of motor oil, a soft duffel bag full of tools, rope (to tie down a bad tire to the luggage rack), jumper cables, tyvek coveralls, gloves, bungee cords, jumper battery, and a towel all relatively neatly stored there and still have room to store the sunroof glass.<P>Even with all of this I was still able to store a couple of small soft side bags of essentials up there when we drove down for the Daytona show.  The rear trunk was full with a suit case, two folding chairs, camera bag, and my wife's cosmetic bag.<p>[This message has been edited by Carrolles (edited 06-06-2001).]||||reg||1
